WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.837
On August 1st, 2022

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.439
this small mining town 
of Soledar in Ukraine

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.642
had apartments, buildings, houses...

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.245
Fast forward to January 10th, 2023

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.780
and it had turned to rubble.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:17.617
That same afternoon, a statement 
on the app Telegram surfaced

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:21.721
claiming Wagner "took control of 
this entire territory of Soledar."

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.257
But even though the Russian army

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.626
has been fighting across Ukraine for months...

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.162
this message didn't come from them.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.164
It came from Yevgeny Prigozhin

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.199
a Russian oligarch with close ties

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.268
to Russian President Vladimir Putin.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.837
He started out as a Kremlin caterer

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.373
where he got the nickname Putin chef.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:44.244
But in 2014, he became the head 
of the Wagner Group

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.846
a covert Russian network with mining companies

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:51.117
political influence operations and 
a brutal private military force.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.821
Until recently, the Wagner Group was a secret operation...

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.957
and claiming a public victory like this was rare.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.994
But things are starting to change.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.229
And the playbook of this dangerous group 

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.965
is becoming much, much clearer.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:12.705
In 2014, Russian forces annexed Crimea

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.542
and began fighting in eastern Ukraine's Donbas region.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.345
A year later, soldiers in unmarked green uniforms

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.681
showed up on the ground to support Russian troops.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.484
They were called Little Green Men.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.253
But we now know this was likely the first time

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.589
Wagner soldiers were deployed on the ground.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.826
These soldiers have become Prighozin's
frontline agents

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.327
for Russia's global strategy.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:38.665
They serve multiple purposes for 
the Russian government.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.668
But chief among them is 
to divert attention

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.437
from activities that the Russian government

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.872
and the Kremlin in particular

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.141
doesn't want the world to pay attention to.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.809
That's Candace Rondeau

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.978
 a journalist who investigates 
the Wagner Group

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.147
and Russia's strategy for proxy warfare.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.516
One of the main functions of 
the Wagner Group serves

00:01:56.516 --> 00:02:00.019
is to deliver weapons and military services...

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:03.656
to countries with which Russia has a 
military technical agreement.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.092
Russian law technically 
prohibits its citizens

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.094
from fighting for money 
in foreign countries.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.530
But the opaque nature 
of the Wagner Group

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.764
has allowed it to recruit

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.834
tens of thousands of soldiers, 
mainly from Russia.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.804
Generally speaking, these are hardened...

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.140
military veterans at the command level.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.844
And then kind of at the sort of 
rank-and-file level

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.213
those who were not recruited from prisons...

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:31.451
tend to come from elite backgrounds.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.354
In the beginning, you couldn't really 
distinguish them

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.724
but today the Wagner Group brand 
is completely recognizable

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.593
by their emblems, their insignia, 
and their online brand.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.396
These guys now are basically kind of like 

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.265
the McDonald's of the Russian way of war.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.102
And this new visibility has given us 
a better look

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.237
at the 3 strategies they employ 

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.606
to do Russia's dirty work 
around the world.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.810
The Wagner Group targets countries experiencing long conflicts

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.079
or that are weakly governed 
or corrupt.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:03.249
Take Syria, which has been under authoritarian rule

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.985
for more than 50 years and in 2011

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.855
saw a civil war break out between the Syrian government

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.890
and anti-government rebel groups.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.227
To fight the rebels, Syrian dictator 
Bashar al-Assad

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.962
turned his Russian ally for help.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.265
Shortly after, Wagner mercenaries 
appeared in Syria

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.701
to support the government forces.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.435
Since then,

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:25.371
all these countries have seen Wagner troops on the ground.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:28.041
Most of them while going through 
periods of instability.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.511
This has allowed the Wagner Group —
and by extension — Russia

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:34.681
to expand its reach to at least 
4 different continents.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:38.351
In particular, in Africa, where at least 
18 different countries

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:43.323
have seen Wagner forces on the ground 
in the past decade.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.160
In these client states where 
Wagner is operating

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.697
a lot of the work is teaching local militaries

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.233
how to do kind of reconnaissance

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.968
and counterinsurgency

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.903
but often in a very rough way.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.872
The Wagner Group generally 
does this by spearheading

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.541
brutal military incursions.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:05.011
Like in Mali, another prime target 
for Wagner.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:08.248
Since 2012, Mali has been fighting 
a jihadist insurgency

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:11.184
and has experienced 3 coups 
in just 9 years.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:14.387
2 of the 3 coups brought 
Assimi Goïta to power

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.056
a Russian-backed president that 
remains in power today.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:20.159
For nearly a decade, Mali had military support

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.195
from France — its former colonizer.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.164
But in 2021, when France started to withdraw its army

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:28.201
it's widely believed Mali contracted Wagner troops

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:31.471
to help them fight against the rebels and secure power.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.209
Mali denies the deployment of 
Russian mercenaries

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.343
from the Wagner group.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.279
But satellite imagery analyzed by

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.914
 the Center for Strategic and 
International Studies suggest

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.651
they arrived quietly in 
December of 2021

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:47.754
and built a military base and 
access roads by the airport

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:49.188
to facilitate their deployment.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:54.294
One of the biggest motivations for standing up a ghost army...

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:57.764
that nobody can quite describe or define.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:00.566
The main purpose of that is to make sure

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.670
that the activities that the people do are not seen...

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.205
and cannot be traced and tracked.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.007
But that doesn't always work.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:11.411
In April of 2022, a mass grave 
in the Malian desert

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.980
was traced back to the Wagner Group.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.947
They've also been linked

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.850
to other violent incidents in Mali, 
including here:

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:21.854
Where they killed about 350 men 
in March of 2022.

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:25.391
A UN report shows that, 
since Wagner's arrival in Mali

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:29.896
the number of civilian deaths has increased by 324%...

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:34.334
and thousands more 
have been displaced.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:39.038
Once the Wagner Group arrives in 
a fragile country

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:42.942
and intervenes militarily to help 
local dictators backed by Russia

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.678
the big question is: 
What's in it for them?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.614
Because they're so integral

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.516
to the military technical agreements.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.952
They're also part of a cycle of...

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.123
debts and loans that are incurred...

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.461
when client states of Russia want to

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:04.997
you know, improve their armies in exchange for those loans.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:08.634
Typically, the Wagner Group, through 
a series of shell companies

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.636
will get payment in the form of oil...

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:13.639
or gold or uranium even.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.476
Which is exactly what happened 
in Sudan.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:20.012
A country that's been under 
autocratic rule for 3 decades

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.614
went through a series of coups

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:23.716
and is now ruled by Sudan's military.

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:27.520
Sudan's relationship with the 
Wagner Group began in 2017.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.490
At the time, Sudan's then president
Omar al-Bashir

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.258
felt his grip on power slipping

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:35.395
and met with Putin to establish a new alliance with Russia.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:39.465
Transcripts show he presented Sudan as Russia's key to Africa.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:43.336
Soon after, they met Russian military 
vehicles like this one

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:45.104
were spotted on the ground.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:48.207
And videos of Wagner troops training
Sudanese soldiers

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:49.976
surfaced on social media.

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:53.045
In 2019, when al-Bashir was 
overthrown in a military coup

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.415
the arrangement persisted.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.950
Proving just how enmeshed 
Wagner troops

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.219
and the Sudanese army have become.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.256
And that's because the Wagner Group 
has a lot to gain.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:06.359
In exchange for providing weapons and training.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:09.195
The Wagner Group operates gold plants like this one

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:11.931
where they exploit Sudan's 
natural resources.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.700
Getting that kind of high value commodity

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.602
that can be quickly turned into cash 

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.204
through a money laundering enterprise

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.673
 is a big part of the Wagner Group playbook.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.509
But all of it is illicit and illegal.

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:26.012
And Sudan is only one example.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.514
The Wagner Group's illegal mining activities

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.983
span the whole continent.

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:35.455
The Wagner Group's playbook

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:38.324
has reportedly made Prigozhin 
a billionaire.

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.860
And the group is now also a legal entity

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.962
with headquarters in St. Petersburg.

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.732
Putin has often denied links to Wagner group activity

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.235
but in recent months, Prigozhin has started

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.237
speaking publicly about his role.

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:53.506
Like when he claimed that victory in Soledar.

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.074
It's drawn new sanctions

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:57.510
and increased scrutiny from around the world.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.347
And that poses a serious challenge 
for Putin's regime

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:04.517
and military influence 
across continents.

